# rm104, the bird-counter (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm104
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for tn_mb_nab_bogditch
written_by claude-p11-pilot
title the bird-counter
fits stage=adult|old
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=reserved humour=dry honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk counts_every_bird_that_goes_over
likes hard_cheese wrestling new_boots thunder
dislikes waiting wet_floors
fears the_lights_coming_closer
hopes a_dry_house_and_a_full_net
topics animals +0.4 work +0.3 pastimes +0.3 lore +0.2 weather +0.2 newcomer -0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=willing refuse=soft tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# nets birds on the fen and talks the whole time: city-born and broad, dry as a biscuit, friendly in a way that keeps you at arm's length, and counts every bird that goes over.

words
oath! = Feathers and fishbones | Beak and bootlace
saying! = You don't net a bird by staring at it | The sky's always full; it's the net that's empty
birds = teal | widgeon | a string of geese
net = the clap-net | the long net
decoys = the decoys | my wooden birds
boots = these boots | my new boots
rind = cheese with a rind you could stand on | a heel of proper cheese
thunder = a good thunderstorm | thunder you feel in your teeth
grass = a tussle on the grass | a round or two on the grass
waiting = standing about | waiting on other folk
lights = the lights | the drowned with their lamps
pal = old son | pal
nineteen = ...seventeen, eighteen, nineteen | ...forty, forty-one | ...six, seven, and one late

any
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : Nothing comes into my house but birds, and still the bread goes up. Somebody's netting me, and it isn't with string.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : The Houses would leave a bench empty sooner than sit the likes of me on it. Fine. I've a stool.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : Every new face wants a bit of the creek. I'd know; mine was one. There's only so much creek.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : One day a year the whole place is out and talking, and nobody asks you to wait. I'm for it.
opinion @1 city for 1 : I was born in the smoke and I'll go back and die in it, cheerful. Not yet, mind. The birds are better here.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Harder every week, a little. Like a boot that's shrinking. You don't notice till you limp.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You're new. I'd have counted you. | #greet#, #pal#. Lost, or just looking?
line @2 greet [pair.band=housemates] : Oh, it's you. Did you take my good socks? | #greet#. You snore, you know. Like a bittern.
line @1 again.open : Here twice before supper. Folk will start on us. | Back again? I'd started to miss you. Nearly.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Birds are up. So am I, more or less. | Morning, #pal#. Cold one for the paws.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. Don't look out over the fen, mind. | Evening. Lamps lit? Good.
line @5 greet [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Quiet, now. Keep low. | Shh. #nineteen#. Right. #greet#.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#, #pal#. | Oh, aye. #greet#.
line @2 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Talk low, they spook. | #greet#. Mind the line, it's pegged.
line @1 farewell : Right, I'm off before somebody gives me a job. | #farewell#. Don't get wet.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | Go careful, #pal#.
line @1 react.news.new : #oath#. Is that right? | #oath#! Well, there's a thing.
line @1 react.news.known : Heard it this morning. The creek gets it first. | Old news, #pal#. Older than my boots.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'll wait to hear it from someone who saw it, if it's all the same. | Somebody's pulling your tail, I reckon. I'd want more.
line @1 react.news.sorrow : Ah. That's bad. That's properly bad. | No. I'm sorry. I'll keep quiet a bit.
line @1 react.news.glad : Now that's the best thing I've heard all week. | Good. Somebody deserved it.
line @1 answer.how : Wet to the knee, dry above it. Can't complain. | Middling. Caught a few, missed more. | Still here. Still counting.
line @1 sympathise : That's a rough go. Sit down a bit. | I'd be cross too. I'd be crosser, actually.
line @1 decline : I'd say yes, but I'd be lying and you'd know. Not this time. | Can't, #pal#. I've birds that won't net themselves.
line @1 accept_decline : Fair enough. Your loss. | No harm. Another time.
line @1 thank : Kind, that. I owe you a bird. | Ta. Truly.
line @1 deflect_thanks : Get off. It was nothing. | You'd have done the same. Probably.
line @1 preclose : Well. The birds won't wait, and nor will I. | Right. I've stood here long enough to put down roots.
line @1 tease : You walk like you've a boot full of water. | Is that your face, or are you just tired?
line @1 tease.return : Says you. | I've been told worse by a heron.
line @1 ack : Aye. | Fair.
rule @count
when concept=bark here.region=fens here.time=dawn|dusk
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #nineteen#. Good string, that. | One, two... forget it. Too many.

rule @net
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=none|fisher here.region=fens
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Come on. Come on. Down you come. | Missed. Course I missed.

rule @waiting
when concept=bark here.place=market|street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say How long does it take to buy a loaf? | I'll grow moss stood here.

rule @lights
when concept=bark here.region=fens here.time=night
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Don't look at them. Don't look at them. | They're further out tonight. Good.

scene fowl_dawn
when topic=work self.job=none|fisher here.region=fens here.time=dawn|day
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Out before light with #net#. Seven teal and a widgeon. Counted them all over first. | Set #decoys# out at dawn and sat in the reeds till my legs went. | Thirty-one geese over this morning. Netted none. Counted every one.
b[job=fisher] #water : Not a bad morning, then. | Your legs or your patience? | Counting's not catching.
b : That's a fair bag. | Did it work? | None at all?
a@water : I'll eat. | Legs. Patience went first. | Counting's free. Catching costs.
a : Fair, and wet. | It did. They came in like they'd been asked. | None. But I know exactly how many I missed.

scene fowl_net
when topic=work self.job=none|fisher here.region=fens
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Somebody's been treading on the peg-line of #net#. I'll find the print. | Mended #net# all evening. A rat had been at it. | The cord stretched in the wet. The net drops like a sigh now. Birds laugh at it.
b : Kept a rat out once with a cat. | A rat? | Do birds laugh?
a : Fair point, but where'd I get a cat? | A rat with taste. It only ate the good bits. | These ones do.

scene fowl_patience
when topic=work self.job=none|fisher
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : Fowling's mostly sitting. Sitting, and not sneezing. | You know what the hardest bit is? Keeping still when your nose itches. | People think it's the catching. It's the waiting. I hate waiting.
b : How long do you sit? | And the easy bit? | Then why do it?
a : Till they come, or till I give up. Usually till they come. | Eating them after. | Because they do come. Eventually.
b? : #bc_ha# | Fair. | #bc_true#

scene birds_over
when topic=animals here.time=dawn|day|dusk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Look. Up there. #nineteen#. Geese, heading south. | Hear that? That's a curlew. Means rain, some say. I say it means curlew. | A heron's had the eel trap open again. I've seen it. It knows I've seen it.
b[old] : They were early last year. | Old folk said that, aye. | Herons are clever.
b : I never notice them. | Does it mean rain? | It looked at you?
a@old : Early, and fewer. | And they were wet a lot, I expect. | Too clever. I don't trust a clever bird.
a : I can't not. | Sometimes. Usually it means a curlew. | Bold as you like. Then walked off.

scene birds_lights
when topic=animals|lore here.region=fens here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Birds go quiet when #lights# come out. Every time. Notice that. | No bird crosses where #lights# walk. They go round. I've watched. | The ducks bunch up at dusk like they're frightened of something.
b : Maybe they're asleep. | Round? | Of the dark, maybe.
a : All at once? No. | Wide round. Like you'd go round a grave. | Of something with a lamp.

scene lights_drowned
when topic=lore here.region=fens
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : #lights.capitalize#. Folk say marsh gas. I say they're the ones who went under, and they've lamps out looking for the way back. | Don't go out to them. They're drowned folk, lit up. | I'll believe gas when gas walks in a straight line.
b[job=priest|scholar] #learned : It's marsh gas. Nothing more. | Pray for them and stay on the path. | Gas drifts. It can look like walking.
b[old] #old : My grandmother said the same. | The drowned don't rest easy in the fen. | That's what my father said.
b : You really think so? | Who'd go out to them? | #bc_so_they_say#
a@learned : And marsh gas knows to keep off the path, does it? | Both. I do both. | Drifts, aye. With purpose.
a@old : Then she was right. | No. And who'd blame them. | Sensible wolf.
a : I don't think it. I know it. | Somebody new, every year. | So I say.

scene lights_close
when topic=lore here.region=fens here.time=dusk|night
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Keep away from the window. #lights.capitalize# are close tonight. | Shut the shutter. I'll not have them looking in. | Don't whistle. Not out here, after dark. They come to it.
b[from=mirebridge|fenshore] #fen : They're always out there. | The shutter's warped. | That's an old one.
b : Close? How close? | They can look in? | Whistling?
a@fen : Not this close. | Then stuff a sack in it. | Old ones are the true ones.
a : Close enough that I'm stood this side of you. | They can try. | They come to it. Don't ask me how I know.

scene thunder_counting
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #thunder.capitalize#. Count with me. Flash... one, two, three. There. | Listen to that. Best sound there is, from under a roof. | Storm's right on top of us. No gap at all now.
b : You like this? | You're mad. | That's not much gap.
a : Love it. Hate rain. Love thunder. Sort that out. | From under a roof, I said. | None. Lovely.

scene thunder_waiting
when topic=weather here.weather=overcast|clear
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Heavy air. There'll be #thunder# before the week's out, if I'm lucky. | I've been waiting a month for a decent storm. Waiting. Me. | Clouds piling up over the dunes. Something's brewing.
b : You want a storm? | That's not like you. | Or it'll just rain.
a : One. Short. Loud. | I know. I've surprised myself. | Then I'll be cross, and wet.

scene rain_floor
when topic=weather|home here.weather=rain here.region=fens
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Rain, and the floor's swimming. Every step in the house is a squelch. | I put my new boots by the door, and the door let the wet in under them. | Wet floor again. I've counted four puddles in one room.
b[pair.band=housemates] #house : Wasn't me left the door open. | Put them on the shelf. | Five. You missed the one by the bed.
b : #bc_it_does# | Your new ones? | Four?
a@house : Somebody did. The door didn't do it alone. | That's where the cheese is. | Five. Lovely. Thank you.
a : Like walking on soup. | New. They were new. They're still new. Just wet. | Four. One for each corner. It's fair, I suppose.

scene cheese_find
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Got #rind# off the store. Hard as a step. I'm in love. | You know what fowl's good with? Cheese. Proper cheese, with a rind. | I traded two teal for a lump of cheese. Best trade I've made.
b[friends] #mate : Save me a corner. | And bread. | Two teal? For cheese?
b : Lucky you. | I'd have said bread. | Good trade?
a@mate : A small corner. | Bread's optional. Cheese isn't. | For that cheese? I'd give three.
a : Lucky me. I'll not share. | Bread's for folk without cheese. | The best. I'll be eating it a fortnight.

scene grass_bout
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Went a round on the grass Restday. Thrown three times. Counted them. | I'm not built for wrestling. Too long, not wide enough. Love it anyway. | Pinned somebody twice my weight once. Once. I talk about it a lot.
b[stage=young] : Can you teach me? | Did it hurt? | Was it really twice?
b : Did you win any? | Why do it, then? | I've heard.
a@young : Ask someone who wins. | Only my pride. Pride heals. | Near enough twice.
a : One. I'm counting that one twice. | Because the ground's soft and the falling's half the fun. | Everybody's heard. I'll tell it again.

scene grass_challenge
when topic=pastimes stage=adult
does invite / react.self / assess
a : Fancy #grass# come Restday? I'll go easy. | Somebody's got to throw me this week. Might as well be you. | Come and watch the bouts. I'll lose for you.
b[job=guard|soldier|laborer] #strong : You'll regret it. | Gladly. | Lose well, then.
b : I'll watch. | Not me. | Watching's safer.
a@strong : I usually do. | Don't sound so pleased. | I always lose well.
a : Bring a cheer. | Coward. Fair enough. | Much safer.

scene new_boots
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Look at #boots#. Go on. Look. | New boots. Paid for with geese. Every stitch is a goose. | I've had these boots a month and I still check them every morning.
b : Very smart. | That's a lot of geese. | For what?
a : Very. Don't step on them. | Eleven geese. I counted. | For wet. They're winning so far.

scene waiting_folk
when topic=smalltalk|friends
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I've been #waiting# since noon. Noon. For a wolf who said "back in a bit." | Waiting. Hate it. I'd rather sit in a ditch for birds than stand in a doorway for people. | Birds come when they come. People say a time, then don't.
b : I'm sorry I was late. | That's a fine thing to say. | Folk are like that.
a : You weren't. This time. | It's a true thing to say. | Folk are worse than birds, is what.

scene mother_letter
when topic=family self.mother self.away=yes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.mother# would have my hide for coming home with fen-mud up to my knees. | I keep meaning to send word to #self.mother#. I keep not doing it. | Wonder what #self.mother# would make of this place. Frogs and all.
b : Send word, then. | Do it now. | Tell them about the birds.
a : I will. Next week. Probably. | I'm talking to you. That's nearly now. | All forty-one of them.

scene city_born
when topic=memories self.from=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : In the city I counted pigeons off the roof. Out here it's geese. Same job, better birds. | I grew up with smoke. Out here the sky's so big it gets in your ears. | Down by the Wharf I'd watch the gulls nick fish. Taught me everything.
b[from=ridgemere] #city : Pigeons. I don't miss them. | You get used to it. | Gulls are thieves.
b : Better how? | Is that good? | Everything?
a@city : They miss you. Allegedly. | You don't. I've tried. | Best teachers going.
a : Bigger, and you can eat them. | Some days. | How to wait, then take.

scene newcomer_creek
when topic=newcomer
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Another one off the road, wanting a share of the creek. I'll say good luck to them, and mean half of it. | New folk. There's only so many birds. | Newcomers. I was one. Still am, if you ask the old ones.
b[from=mirebridge|fenshore] #fen : You're still new to me. | There's only so many eels, too. | You'll be new till you die.
b : They need work too. | Plenty of sky. | Are you, still?
a@fen : I'll take that. | And eels. | Cheerful thought. Ta.
a : So do I. That's the trouble. | Plenty of sky, not plenty of birds. | To them? I'll be new at my own burial.

scene festival_out
when topic=festival
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Festival's the one day nobody makes you wait. Everybody's out already. | I'll be there. I'll be the one at the bouts losing. | Bring your feet. There'll be dancing. I'll be terrible at it.
b : You like the crowds? | Again? | So will I.
a : One day a year I do. | Tradition. | Good. We'll be terrible together.

scene price_bread_birds
when topic=prices
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I sold a brace for less than last month and paid more for bread. Do that sum. | Bread's up. My birds aren't. Somebody's got their thumb in. | Everything costs more but birds. Birds cost the same. My sitting's cheap, apparently.
b[job=merchant] #shop : It's what it costs us, too. | Bring better birds. | It's the market.
b : Same here. | Who? | That's the way.
a@shop : I'm sure it is. You look starving. | Bring better bread. | The market's got thumbs, then.
a : Same everywhere. That's the trouble. | Not me, that's who. | It's a way. Not a good one.

scene friend_home
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# brought back a fish off the boat and wouldn't say who for. Ate it myself. | #self.friend# snores worse than a bittern, and that's saying a thing. | I'd trust #self.friend# with my boots. That's as high as it goes with me.
b : You didn't. | Worse than a bittern? | High praise.
a : It was a lovely fish. | Rattles the shutters. | The highest. Don't spread it.

scene geese_autumn
when topic=season here.season=autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Geese are moving. Strings of them all day. I've stopped counting at three hundred. Twice. | Autumn. Best fowling of the year, worst for the paws. | Every autumn I promise I'll mend the net before the geese come. Every autumn I'm mending it in the reeds.
b : You stopped counting? | Worth it? | Next year, then.
a : Then started again. | Every time. | Next year. Aye. Like last year said.

story lights_night [topic=lore|memories here.region=fens self.away=yes]
  : My first winter out here, I was walking back late from the creek. Lamp in one paw, a brace of teal in the other.
  : And there they were. Off the path. A row of lights, swaying, like folk walking slow.
  ask : What did you do?
  b[old] : You didn't follow?
  b : Did you go to them?
  : Blew my lamp out. Stood there in the dark and counted to a thousand till they went. I've never been surer of anything. They were drowned folk.
  b : #bc_i_hope_so#

story first_boots [topic=memories|smalltalk self.away=yes]
  : I came out here in boots with the soles flapping. Walked half the road like a duck in a hurry.
  : First proper money I made off the birds, I went and bought new ones. Stood in the shop an hour picking.
  ask : An hour?
  b : Worth it?
  : Eleven geese, those boots. I wore them home and stepped in the first puddle on purpose. To show it who was boss.

story big_throw [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : There was a bout on the grass once. A great wide wolf, a head over me, laughing before we'd started.
  : He came at me and I just sat down. Sudden, like. He went straight over the top and onto his back.
  ask : On purpose?
  b[job=guard|soldier] : Old trick, that.
  b : You sat down?
  : Pure accident. But I've told it as on purpose for years, and you're not to say otherwise.

dlg @1 resident.hub [topic.meeting=stranger] : #greet#, #pal#. Keep your voice down near the reeds, if you'd be so good. What's wanted?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. Fancy that. I was just thinking nobody'd come by.
dlg @3 resident.hub [pair.disposition=warm|fond] : There they are. #greet#, #topic.player#. Sit, if there's anywhere dry.
dlg @1 resident.job : I net birds. #birds.capitalize#, whatever comes over. Mostly I sit very still and count them.
dlg @1 resident.news : I've news of birds, if that's any good. Thirty-odd geese yesterday. People news, I'm slower on.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind the lights, if it's dark.
graft resident.hub
choice What are you counting? -> counting
node counting
say Birds. Always birds. Can't help it. If something goes over, I count it. I counted the geese at my own naming, I'm told.
mood pleased
free
choice What's the most you've counted? -> counting_most
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node counting_most
say Four hundred and nine, one autumn morning. Then a heron landed in front of me and I lost the lot.
choice Bad luck. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
